{
  "info": {
    "name": "Devclothes E-commerce API",
    "description": "This collection contains pre-configured requests for testing all Devclothes API routes, including authorization, products, banners, notifications, and Stripe payments.\n\n### How to Use:\n1. Import this file into Postman (**File** -> **Import** -> Select this file).\n2. Keep your backend running on `http://localhost:5000` (or adjust the `baseUrl` variable in the collection variables if different).\n3. Run **Register** or **Login**. The login script automatically extracts the JWT token and saves it to the `jwtToken` collection variable, which is automatically attached as a Bearer Token to all protected requests.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Authentication",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register User",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"john@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const response = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (response.token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"jwtToken\", response.token);",
                  "    console.log(\"JWT token saved to collection variables!\");",
                  "} else if (pm.cookies.has(\"authToken\")) {",
                  "    // If token is stored in HTTPOnly cookies, Postman handles it automatically, ",
                  "    // but we can also set the variable just in case.",
                  "    const token = pm.cookies.get(\"authToken\");",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"jwtToken\", token);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"john@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
